It is stated that mother of the Appellant is undergoing treatment from BM Rakesh Kumar Sood vs The State (Nct Of Delhi) on 16 February, 2024 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/37758096/
1 Gupta Hospital Pvt. Ltd. and the Doctor has diagnosed her to be a case of bulky/prominent Hila vascular and was advised Dobutamine stress echo for further management, apart from being a case of fracture proximal femur.
4. Considering the fact that mother of the Appellant, who is over 85 years of age, is suffering from various ailments including those of spine and lungs and her health condition is deteriorating, as indicated from the medical documents placed on record, which have been verified to be genuine by the State, this Court is inclined to grant interim suspension of sentence to the Appellant for a period of eight weeks from the date of his release,subject to his furnishing a personal bond in the sum of Rs.25,000/- with one surety of like amount, to the satisfaction of learned Trial Court and further subject to the following conditions:-
(i) Appellant will not leave the country without prior permission of this Court;
(ii) He shall not indulge in any criminal activity or communicate with or come in contact with the Victim or any other person associated with the present case;
(iii) He shall provide his permanent residential address to the concerned IO and shall intimate the IO as well as this Court by filing an affidavit regarding any change in the residential address;
This is a digitally signed order.
